  "result": "The classic off-by-1000 bug: JWT `exp` is in **seconds** since epoch, but `Date.now()` returns **milliseconds**.\n\n```js\n// Wrong \u2014 compares milliseconds to seconds, token appears to never expire\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp) { ... }\n\n// Fix \u2014 convert to the same unit\nif (Date.now() / 1000 > payload.exp) { ... }\n// or equivalently\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp) { ... }\n```\n\nA token with `exp: 1713657600` (a Unix timestamp in seconds) looks like it expires in the year **55,000+** when compared against `Date.now()` (~1.7 trillion ms), so the check `Date.now() > payload.exp` is always false \u2014 every token passes.\n\nIf you share the middleware file I can apply the fix directly.",
